Local changes: src/unicast.rs only (src/lib.rs and src/utils.rs are byte-identical to the crates.io 1.8.0 copy; sha256 of the three files is checked by hand when the patch is refreshed). Upstream lets one read task and one write task sit inside the same rustls Connection at the same time: `inner: UnsafeCell<TlsStream<TcpStream>>` is guarded by two different mutexes (`read_mtx` / `write_mtx`), so both `&mut TlsStream` accesses can be live at once. rdog saw roughly 9% of fresh TLS links lose their first query, with `TX task failed: handshake not complete` on the server side (see the RAI-524 ledger entry and PR #178). The local change puts every access to the connection — read, write, flush, shutdown — behind one `tls_mtx`, and never holds it across an await: each critical section does one non-blocking poll and, on `Pending`, releases the lock and parks on this link's own waker (a `Semaphore`, so a wake that arrives before the waiter registers is not lost). `read_gate` / `write_gate` keep one whole `read_exact` / `write_all` call from being interleaved with another call in the same direction. `close()` flushes the accepted records with a bounded 5s deadline and reports an error instead of returning success while bytes are still buffered, then cancels a `CancellationToken` that wakes every parked task. Nothing outside `src/unicast.rs` is modified.
Removal condition: delete this directory and the `[patch.crates-io]` entry in the repository `Cargo.toml` once an upstream release guarantees that reads and writes never enter one `Connection` concurrently (`Connection::reader()/writer()` split or an equivalent lock). Upstream report draft: `docs/`-free copy kept in the captain drive under `handoffs/RAI-524/upstream-issue-draft.md`; the rdog side owns the send decision.
